      "content": "Thanks for the feedback. I was wondering about the genre split though. You put Marcus, Andre, and Kenji into different categories or \"versatile\" buckets, while Julian, Elena, and Arthur felt very much like the \"prestige\" group.\n\nI'm curious if you're noticing a pattern there regarding the characters' backgrounds. Like, is there a reason you feel the 'street-smart' or 'tech' characters don't naturally land in a high-society setting compared to the others? Is it just about their current occupation, or is there more of a demographic thing at play in how these archetypes usually function in Hollywood?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
